Package: txschools
Title: Polite, Reproducible Access to Texas Education Agency Public Performance Data
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R:
    person(given = "David",
           family = "Kahle",
           role = c("aut", "cre"),
           email = "david.kahle@gmail.com")
Description: Tools for discovering, downloading, caching, parsing, and citing
    public school-performance data published by the Texas Education Agency
    (TEA): the Texas Academic Performance Reports (TAPR, 2013 onward,
    including the statewide advanced-download data files and variable
    dictionaries), per-campus School Report Cards (SRC, 2004-2019), the
    Academic Excellence Indicator System (AEIS, 2004-2012), and PEIMS
    fund/function/object-level district and charter financial data
    (budgets and actuals, 1999-2000 onward), and school district property
    tax rates (Texas Comptroller and TEA adopted-rate workbooks, 2005-06
    onward) with an interactive district tax-rate map viewer, plus a
    name-to-identifier directory of Texas campuses and districts and
    helpers joining districts to Census geography. Downloads
    happen on demand against TEA's public pages; files are cached locally
    under 'tools::R_user_dir()' with source-URL, timestamp, and checksum
    metadata. TEA masking and suppression values are preserved exactly.
    This package is not affiliated with TEA and does not redistribute TEA
    datasets.
